# Jihad Browser preferences UI package. Copyright 2026 NotAlexNoyle. MPL-2.0 (matches the
# GRE it registers into).
#
# Backs about:preferences and about:settings — see
# render/goanna/components/jihadAboutPreferences.js, which resolves both to
# chrome://jihad-prefs/content/preferences.html.
#
# A chrome:// package, not a resource:// one, on purpose: the page must load with the
# system principal so it can write through Services.prefs, and chrome:// is what gives
# it that. Content is unable to reach it because the about: module does not set
# URI_SAFE_FOR_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: the "content" part of the path is not decoration. nsChromeProtocolHandler
# calls SetOwner(systemPrincipal) only when the chrome url path begins "/content/", so
# chrome://jihad-prefs/content/preferences.html gets the system principal and can write
# Services.prefs. Rename that segment and the page silently loses its privileges — every
# pref call throws and the page renders as an empty settings screen. (Found in review
# 2026-08-06; the flag on the about: module is what keeps CONTENT out, this is what lets
# the PAGE in. Two different mechanisms, both required.)
#
# Paths are relative to THIS FILE, which is installed at the GRE root next to
# chrome.manifest (same arrangement as jihad-branding.manifest).
content jihad-prefs prefsui/content/

# about:reader?url=… (T-642) and about:desktopsite?on=…&url=… (T-645). Two components of this
# package rather than of render/goanna/components/: each is the about: module for a name of
# its own and is used only with the files beside it. Each file's header says what it does.
# about:reader's page is content/reader.html, served UNPRIVILEGED (the module sets
# URI_SAFE_FOR_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT, so the chrome channel's system principal is dropped).
component {b7a1c3e2-5d94-4f08-8a6b-3e2f9c7d1a54} prefsui/content/jihadAboutReader.js
contract @mozilla.org/network/protocol/about;1?what=reader {b7a1c3e2-5d94-4f08-8a6b-3e2f9c7d1a54}
component {2c9e6f41-7b3a-4d85-9e10-6a4b8d2f5c37} prefsui/content/jihadSiteMode.js
contract @mozilla.org/network/protocol/about;1?what=desktopsite {2c9e6f41-7b3a-4d85-9e10-6a4b8d2f5c37}
